257
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:58,372
I don't know what's going on, but cheers!

258
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,860
I'm confused too, but cheers!

259
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:04,960
45 degrees!

260
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,677
I won't turn back.

261
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:24,717
Not after coming so far.

262
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,217
I may have been sidetracked for a while.

263
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:29,117
But I'm headed straight forward again.

264
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,177
All the way around the world.

265
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,377
Back to Twin Cape.

266
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:33,837
So far away.

267
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:36,337
Because I know you'll be waiting for me.

268
00:16:36,420 --> 00:16:38,417
And I have to keep my promise.

269
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,857
Both to you and my crew.

270
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:43,097
So I will see this to the end.

271
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:44,177
No matter what.

272
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:46,200
So wait for me.

273
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,480
Just a little bit longer.

274
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:03,900
Hey, Le Boon, what's wrong?

275
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:18,577
Well, you seem to be
in high spirits today.

276
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:19,700
I wonder why.

277
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:30,617
Take a look at this a wanted poster you
mean you already have a bounty on you

278
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:36,420
Pardon me for not introducing myself properly
before I am known as Dead Bones Brook

279
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:41,977
And I'm a wanted man my nickname
is the humming swordsman

280
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:46,057
I have a bounty of 33 million
berries On my head I was the

281
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:49,557
leader of a battle convoy in the
kingdom of my origin afterwards

282
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:52,937
I served As a musician and
swordsman in the rumbar pirates

283
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:55,757
later succeeding yorkie as
captain of the crew Until their

284
00:17:55,840 --> 00:18:01,077
demise but now I pledge my
life and my services to Captain

285
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:05,697
Monkey D Luffy of the Straw Hat
Pirates I shall do my best to

286
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:11,820
make you proud that is to say
I shall work myself to the bone

287
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,590
All right!

288
00:18:16,673 --> 00:18:17,520
One more toast!

289
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:18,818
Raise your glasses!

290
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:34,250
How splendid.

291
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:36,360
Thank you, Franky Usopp.

292
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:37,500
It's perfect.

293
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:38,980
No problem, bro.

294
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:41,257
I can make one of these
any day of the week.

295
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:43,297
But it was my design, just so you know.

296
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:45,439
Yeah, but I picked out the flowers.

297
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:49,480
But truly, it's a beautiful memorial.

298
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:51,557
And this is certainly for the best,

299
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:54,417
since I could scarcely bring
all of those bones onto Mr.

300
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:55,330
Lion with me.

301
00:18:55,413 --> 00:18:58,260
Okay, but it's Thousand
Sunny, not Mr. Lion.

302
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:00,540
You know, by happy coincidence?

303
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:03,357
Thriller Bark originally
came from the West Blue.

304
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,146
just like the Rumbar Pirates.

305
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:07,637
Despite the troubles this ship brought me,

306
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:11,779
I hope my friends will rest peacefully
in the soil of their homeland.

307
00:19:13,980 --> 00:19:15,617
We're gonna head back now Brooke.

308
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:16,597
We'll see you soon.

309
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:18,260
Glad you like it. Bye-bye.

310
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,390
Thank you

311
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:41,850
Goodness,

312
00:19:41,933 --> 00:19:45,857
you gave me a fright You were out for
quite a while, are you feeling better?

313
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:47,980
Yeah, I overslept a bit

314
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:49,720
And what is that?

315
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:51,520
A dead sword, Yubashiri.

316
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:53,722
I'm laying it to rest here, too.

317
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:00,944
Muffy is the man who
become king of the pirates!

318
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:04,740
Um, what is it?

319
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:06,090
No.

320
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:07,850
Nothing.

321
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:14,551
Oh, in case you hadn't heard,
I officially joined the crew.

322
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:15,830
I see.

323
00:20:15,913 --> 00:20:18,740
Well, that's too bad for
you now, isn't it? Huh?

324
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:23,348
This crew can be a real
handful, that's all.

325
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,200
So it would seem.

326
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:28,497
But I'll give them my blood
and sweat all the same,

327
00:20:28,580 --> 00:20:31,227
except I don't have any
since I'm a skeleton.

328
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:38,073
Zorro's up, so on to our next adventure!

329
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:40,560
Come on, it's time to set sail!

330
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:42,390
Yeah!

331
00:20:44,340 --> 00:20:45,170
Hey!

332
00:20:45,253 --> 00:20:46,697
Zoro, you took off your bandages!

333
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:47,610
Of course I did.

334
00:20:47,693 --> 00:20:49,169
They made it hard to move.

335
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:50,257
That's the point!

336
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:52,357
You're supposed to sit still in a hill!

337
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,270
Come here!

338
00:20:53,353 --> 00:20:54,183
Setting off already?

339
00:20:54,266 --> 00:20:55,857
I'm sorry you can't stick around.

340
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:58,777
Whenever you feel like leaving,
you can take Brooke's ship.

341
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:01,137
I fixed the rudder and the sails for you.

342
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:02,077
It's wonderful.

343
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:04,337
I can't thank you enough
for all you've done.

344
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:07,777
It might take the rest of my life for me
to pay you back, but I'm willing to try.

345
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:10,137
In other words, what do you
say you and I get married?

346
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:12,917
Sorry, babe, you're a champ,
but it won't work out.

347
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,297
I'm afraid I'm just too
super to settle down.

348
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:17,237
I really hate to see you take off.

349
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,877
You sure you don't want to stick
around and party for a few more days?

350
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:20,790
No way!

351
00:21:20,873 --> 00:21:23,877
We're off to Fishman Island, and
it's going to be totally awesome!

352
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:24,790
Fish dudes!

353
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:26,844
There's going to be fish dudes!

354
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:28,297
Screw the fish dudes!

355
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:29,577
There are going to be mermaids!

356
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:31,778
I'm going to flirt with all of them!

357
00:21:32,340 --> 00:21:34,657
I wonder if the mermaids
we encounter would

358
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:36,957
be so gracious as to
show me their panties.

359
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,452
Hey, man, don't be dumb!

360
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,364
Think about what you're saying!

361
00:21:41,060 --> 00:21:43,560
Mermaids don't wear any panties.

362
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:48,157
And I'm telling you,
mermaids are so gorgeous,

363
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:51,887
they even give the pirate empress
Hancock a run for her money.

364
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:54,870
Mermaids, yeah!

365
00:21:54,953 --> 00:21:55,783
Mermaids, yeah!

366
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:58,257
Mermaids are fish from the waist down.

367
00:21:58,340 --> 00:22:00,597
Why do you guys know so
much about Fishman Island?

368
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:03,797
Ah, well, a couple years back before
we got stuck in this hellhole,

369
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:04,717
we took a trip there.

370
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:06,200
You were gonna love it.

371
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:10,137
Wow, Lola, I didn't realize you
went to the New World already.

372
00:22:10,220 --> 00:22:11,877
We didn't go there, you big silly.

373
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:13,457
We came from there in the first place.

374
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:16,011
My mama's a pirate just like me, you know?

375
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,380
Oh, that reminds me.

376
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:20,600
Here, you should take this.

377
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:22,191
It's my mama's Viva card.

378
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:24,020
A piece of paper?

379
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:25,717
Whoa, hang on to that one.

380
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:28,117
One of the greatest pirates
I've ever met in my life.

381
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:29,318
This is Lola's mom.

382
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,277
That'll come in handy someday.

383
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:34,297
Not just anybody gets one of those.

384
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:36,277
Sorry, but what's a Viva card again?

385
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:37,190
What?

386
00:22:37,273 --> 00:22:38,103
You guys don't know?

387
00:22:38,186 --> 00:22:39,757
Come on, Captain, don't be insensitive.

388
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:42,037
They only make Viva
cards in the new world.

389
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:43,532
Oh, I forgot about that.

390
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:45,702
Anyway, this is no normal paper.

391
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:48,497
You can wet it or burn
it, but it won't change.

392
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:51,677
If you take a piece of your fingernail
to the shop where they make these,

393
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:55,677
they'll use it to create a personalized
piece of paper, just like this one.

394
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:59,497
Because of their use, they also call
Viva cards life paper sometimes.

395
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:01,557
The idea is to tear off
a piece and give it to

396
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:04,017
your family or friends
when you go on a journey.

397
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:05,740
Uh-huh. And then what?

398
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:07,390
Take a look.

399
00:23:07,620 --> 00:23:09,973
This is the Viva card I got for my mama.

400
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:13,760
Oh, it's moving!

401
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:17,797
No matter where in the world these scraps
of paper are, they're drawn to each other.

402
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:21,117
So long as I have this, I know
what direction mama is in.

403
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:23,297
It doesn't tell you the
distance, though, I'm afraid.

404
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:24,840
Whoa, that's so neat!

405
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:28,537
I bet there's a bunch of crazy stuff
like that in the new world, huh?

406
00:23:28,620 --> 00:23:31,397
Well, I don't know about crazy,
but it certainly is handy.

407
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:34,797
Anyway, I'm signing the piece of my mama's
Viva card, so if you're ever in trouble,

408
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:37,537
you can use it to find her
and she'll help you out.

409
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:41,137
If that ever happens, be sure to
tell her that I'm doing fine, okay?

410
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:42,500
Wow, thanks, Lola.

411
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:43,500
Hey, hold on.

412
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:45,377
Don't I have one of those already?

413
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:46,290
Huh?

414
00:23:46,373 --> 00:23:50,340
I almost forgot, but Ace gave you
something like this a long time ago.

415
00:23:50,580 --> 00:23:52,051
You remember that, right?

416
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:57,200
That scrap of paper
will reunite us someday.

417
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,680
So that's what it was.

418
00:24:01,300 --> 00:24:02,637
This is it, but...

419
00:24:02,720 --> 00:24:04,097
Huh, that's weird.

420
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:06,886
I thought you said these
things couldn't burn.

421
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:08,521
Are you kidding?

422
00:24:08,660 --> 00:24:09,601
Let me see that!

423
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:16,720
This is definitely a Viva card,

424
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:19,457
but there's something I
neglected to tell you before.

425
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:22,837
The life force of the owner is
also reflected on the paper.

426
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:25,640
Does this belong to someone close to you?

427
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:28,720
Yeah, it's my big brother's.

428
00:24:33,420 --> 00:24:34,250
Lola?

429
00:24:38,020 --> 00:24:44,080
I'm sorry to say this, but your brother's
life is in terrible danger right now.
